    {
      "id": "claim_8b5069c693d54ea4a4cd1e151bf95428",
      "statement": "switch_to_video runs five ordered steps: deactivate reading with turn_off=False to leave lights at their current state, safety-stop a still-running sync, fail out if no entertainment stream is configured, activate the entertainment configuration and connect DTLS (a failed DTLS connect rolls back via deactivate_entertainment_streaming), then start the sync controller and flip the mode to VIDEO.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/mode_manager.py#L78-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3229f30e1632c5c1bb18f4cfaf2b671dc50a26e53fbe9bd91784a2220061ea3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a69ec06ee6484e56aa9fc37c529cdbb8",
      "statement": "switch_to_reading first rejects duplicate calls while _reading_activation_pending is set (returning True as a no-op), fills None xy/brightness from ReadingModeSettings, stops video sync, and—if a connected entertainment stream was just disconnected—sets _reading_activation_pending and schedules _finish_switch_to_reading with GLib.timeout_add(1000, ...) so the bridge finishes deactivating the zone before REST commands; without a stream to disconnect it proceeds synchronously, using time.sleep(0.3) in non-GLIB contexts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/mode_manager.py#L133-L186",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77f6301ad5a500489dc777f6071ffe679155db201da353c50c591ca2a1d5d518:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8a190479540149f08e844953c421ea18",
      "statement": "_finish_switch_to_reading clears the pending flag and then checks for interruption: if current_mode is no longer OFF (e.g., turn_off ran during the delay), it cancels the activation, invokes the callback with False, and stops the GLib timeout; otherwise it calls the reading controller's activate and flips the mode to READING on success.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/mode_manager.py#L188-L223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:727c21a5d6ffd54d9aef905d951345757c84022ee2fc7cf5ee1d1d253c9fc41e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bc936349300a4ae786bc295367956e59",
      "statement": "turn_off cancels any pending reading activation before stopping sync, and because sync_controller.stop() synchronously fires on_video_sync_stopped, it then special-cases the mode transition VIDEO→READING (auto-activation happened) by returning True without touching the lights; only in the non-auto case does it disconnect the stream, deactivate reading, and notify OFF.",
      "evidence": [
